(a) largest |mr_f32 - (mn a_q - mn^2)| / mn over all keys: 2.705e-07; DA's float share is 1.0e-07
    so 4e-6 must absorb |alpha| mn * 1.71e-07: enough while |alpha| mn <= 23 (less what else 4e-6 covers: 3e-8 |q.m|)
(b) rows equal to their cluster's mean (centre int8 with one scale): norm excess, x.mhat - 1, key error |a - a_q|
    allowance: DA = 1.536e-05 per unit of |alpha| mn, plus 4e-6 absolute
